    <selectionEntry name="Decapitator" id="1e2f-7759-ebec-f774" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="unit">
      <categoryLinks>
        <categoryLink name="Independent Character" id="5e53-7406-d75b-13fc" hidden="false" primary="false" targetId="3c96-248b-affd-e504"/>
        <categoryLink name="Infantry" id="71f3-a8de-2abb-d02e" hidden="false" primary="false" targetId="6953-6bba-0bb9-d49d"/>
      </categoryLinks>
      <constraints>
        <constraint id="db9f-174e-f516-db05" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="force" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
      </constraints>
      <costs>
        <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="112"/>
      </costs>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Decapitator" id="d694-9642-f9ed-596a" hidden="false" targetId="203c-c6b0-242a-6678" type="profile"/>
        <infoLink name="Splinter Pistol" id="d409-071d-6972-ac1b" hidden="false" targetId="2970-d6c7-ba60-1ed1" type="profile"/>
      </infoLinks>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Gruesome Talisman" id="c4cd-0378-baba-f74e" hidden="false">
          <description>Models with gruesome talismans count as two models when working out if one side outnumbers the other in close combat. Not that this works against any foe, including Daemons!</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Trophy Rack" id="9894-88f6-7b77-5b8c" hidden="false">
          <description>If a model wtih a trophy rack slays an enemy in close combat, he may chop off their head and stick it onto the trophy rack! This adds +1 to the model&apos;s Leadership for the rest of the battle. Chopping off additional heads has no effect.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Additional Limbs" id="ded0-3551-ca69-5820" hidden="false">
          <description>Two additional arms have been grafted onto Decapitator&apos;s body. These ass +2 to his Attacks characters and +1 to his Weapon Skill, both of which have already been included in his profile.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Decapitator" id="d2a3-27d3-f5e3-747a" hidden="false">
          <description>This is the weapon that has given Decapitator his name. It counts as a power weapon, but if Decapitator rolls a 6 on any of his to hit rolls then that hit is counted as being at double Strength.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Shadow-Skinned" id="307c-d391-d183-c23f" hidden="false">
          <description>The special chameleon-like qualities of Mandrakes allow them to blend into the background, even when they are standing in open terrain. Mandrakes always count as being in cover, giving them a 5+ saving throw against most attakcs. This also applied in assaults, so unless the attackers are armed with frag grenades. Mandrakes will always strike first. If attacked by something that ignores cover then their normal save of 5+ applied.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Master Infiltrator" id="1827-6a02-8bbb-c0c1" hidden="false">
          <description>Decapitator is a supreme master at infiltrating an enemy army. Do not deploy him using the normal rules, even in scenarios that don&apos;t normally allow infiltration to be used. Instead write down where on the table Decapitator is hiding (this must be outside both sides&apos; deployment zones). You may reveal his location at any time by simply showing your opponent Decapitator&apos;s hidden set-up instructions. You must, however, reveal his location on your third turn if you have not done so already.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </selectionEntry>
